  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> be three sets defined as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#8450;</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>}</mo><mo>,</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#8450;</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></math>&nbsp;and</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#8450;</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Then, the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8745;</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8745;</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "is a singleton",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "has exactly two elements",
      "is_correct": false
    },
